[Test]
public void TestPUT_RemoveContract_LastIndexOfX()
{
    var arrList = new ArrayList();
    Assume.True(arrList.Count >= 0);
    int x = PexMethods.ChooseValue(arrList.Cast<int>());

    int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

    arrList.Remove(x);

    int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

    Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX <= New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
}
</code>

The assert statement is checking if the last index of the removed element in the old list is less than or equal to the last index of the same element in the updated list. If the original last index is greater than the updated last index, then this means that the item was inserted at a position greater than the old last index.

Please note that Pex is a fuzz testing tool and might produce different values for each test, hence the use of `Assume.True(arrList.Count >= 0);` and `int x = PexMethods.ChooseValue(arrList.Cast<int>());` to provide input to the test. These lines are necessary to ensure the input values are valid.
